' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention. Exercises bare AND/OR/BITAND/
' BITOR/BITXOR/SHL/SHR and the short-circuit-in-name-only ANDALSO/ORELSE
' (this substrate does not actually short-circuit either operator today --
' see the ANDALSO/ORELSE case in Fission_X86_64LowerBinOp's own comment
' for the real, disclosed, substrate-wide divergence from the oracle this
' uncovered), all real single-instruction x86 lowerings confirmed directly
' against the oracle (`ArcoFission compile-run`) before being implemented,
' including a real surprise: SHR is, at runtime, actually an ARITHMETIC
' shift right (sign-preserving) despite its own "logical-sounding" name,
' and the separate SAR keyword is not even implemented by the oracle's own
' bytecode VM at all -- confirmed and left as a real, disclosed diagnostic,
' not guessed at.
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
x = 5
y = 10
z = x > 0 AND y > 0
PRINT z
w = x BITAND y
PRINT w
v = x BITOR y
PRINT v
u = x SHL 2
PRINT u
t = x BITXOR y
PRINT t
r = x OR y
PRINT r

a = -8
PRINT a SHR 1
b = 8
PRINT b SHR 1

IF x > 0 ANDALSO y > 0 THEN
    PRINT 100
END IF
IF x < 0 ORELSE y > 0 THEN
    PRINT 200
END IF
